Run, deploy, invoke, bench, snapshot, and inspect TensorWasm Wasm workloads.

Usage: tensor-wasm [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  run          Run a Wasm module locally against the in-process TensorWasm engine
  deploy       Upload a Wasm module to a TensorWasm server
  invoke       Invoke a previously deployed function by id
  bench        Benchmark local invocation latency (P50/P95/P99/max)
  snapshot     Save or restore an instance snapshot
  kernel       Publish, list, or verify entries in the signed kernel registry
  metrics      Fetch and pretty-print Prometheus metrics from a TensorWasm server
  observe      Live operator dashboard over `/healthz` + `/metrics` (refreshes in place)
  serve        Run the TensorWasm HTTP API gateway in-process (binds and serves)
  completions  Emit shell completion scripts for the named shell
  man          Generate roff(7) man pages from the clap command tree
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --tenant <TENANT>
          Tenant id to advertise on outbound API requests via `X-TensorWasm-Tenant`. Zero (the default) suppresses the header for backwards compatibility
          
          [default: 0]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
